Z||000000||Haspers8||05-11-2001||02:15 PM||||   Spent the better part of the mornin at Davenport Racing here in Calgary.  <BR>   Shannon plugged in his fancy scan tool an I guess that my LT1 is operating within spec although he said the right bank O2 sensor is a little lazy.  All in all he said the odd misfire problem is probably the dreaded opti-crap distributor.  <P>Dyno results...  We straped rear control arms down.....MY God they still moved an inch and a half under power.....me no like.  Bushings are on their way, thankfully.  Oh by the way my tach is out by 1000 RPM at 3.  So I bought a tach with a shift light...hehe.<P>DynoJet results<P>Run 1........Run 2<BR>SAE                 <BR>264.1 HP.....269.1 HP <BR>298.5 ft-lbs.299.5 ft-lbs<BR>Uncorrected      <BR>238.8 Hp.....243.0 HP<BR>269.8 ft-lbs.270.4 ft-lbs<P>By the way I saw my first turbo and my first convertible fiero last night at the meeting here in Calgary......Kewllllll.<P>Later <BR>Steve<p>[This message has been edited by Haspers8 (edited 05-11-2001).]||||reg||1
